  "description": "Revised 29-second educational Space Apps trailer. Original Artemis II poster: NASA; independent project without agency/astronaut endorsement. Continuous 30 fps real Unity WebGL gameplay, edited with OpenAI Codex, Python and FFmpeg. Construction sequences play at 4x. Five distinct maps have 0.50-second gameplay cores and nominal 0.07-second transitions (two frames at 30 fps). Greenhouse OFF and ON cases use naturally reached low battery and low food states. Science Facts were earned by actual play; no achievements or scores were fabricated. Game art is AI-created; the ending monitor was edited with built-in imagegen to show classroom drawings. NASA poster was not AI-generated or regenerated. Music: Pastel Twinkles by raincalleer, generated with Suno; song 0a49d446-3f17-465c-8971-c0398cc51905. Supplied 30.01-second track gently fitted to 29 seconds. Historical NASA/CSA references and simplified educational simulation rules. Captured from an isolated current build/profile; mission-selection prerequisites staged only.",
